WEBVTT

NOTE Converted from demo-video-master.srt (MSG/EML Email Viewer for Jira · for Confluence, "The Attachment", 1:52).
NOTE No cue settings: the film keeps its bottom 200 px clear of anything that matters, so the player's default position is right.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.050
[the clock ticks]

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.061
The source of truth for what was agreed

3
00:00:04.061 --> 00:00:06.783
is often an email, attached to a ticket
as a file.

4
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:09.898
And getting at what is inside it
is not easy.

5
00:00:22.048 --> 00:00:24.398
[the clock stops]

6
00:00:24.548 --> 00:00:26.522
It didn't have to be this way.

7
00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:29.198
[tape rewinding]

8
00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:31.769
Same ticket,
with the app installed.

9
00:00:34.016 --> 00:00:36.722
Open the Emails tab,
and there are the minutes.

10
00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:43.606
MSG/EML Email Viewer for Jira renders
every attached .msg and .eml file

11
00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:45.880
as a readable email card,
attachments included.

12
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.606
And a file inside the email

13
00:00:47.606 --> 00:00:50.283
can be attached to the ticket itself,
with one click.

14
00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.321
The app reads each email
from your own Jira,

15
00:00:58.321 --> 00:01:00.455
using the permissions
of whoever is looking,

16
00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:03.170
so nobody sees anything
they weren't already allowed to.

17
00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.158
It becomes readable
in their web browser,

18
00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:07.592
and the app does not store it
anywhere else.

19
00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:12.540
Beyond the service desk, the same app
works on every Jira ticket.

20
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.096
The sidebar shows which emails
are attached,

21
00:01:15.096 --> 00:01:17.007
who attached them, and when.

22
00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:19.485
The Emails tab renders them.

23
00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:30.010
On Confluence, the email viewer
is a macro:

24
00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.375
insert it once,
choose the attached email,

25
00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:35.378
and it renders on the page,
attachments included.

26
00:01:36.768 --> 00:01:39.364
In Jira there is nothing to set up;

27
00:01:39.364 --> 00:01:42.160
on Confluence, you decide
where the email appears.

28
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:48.046
MSG/EML Email Viewer,
for Jira, and for Confluence.

29
00:01:48.046 --> 00:01:51.322
Two new Cloudscript Apps
on the Atlassian Marketplace.

